#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Step 10 Judge: a deterministic pack runs over a window of the run's records, and its sealed Results cite
every record in the window by digest, none missing and none extra, and verify offline.

Usage: 10-judge --population DIR --out RUN/10-judge
       10-judge --population DIR --preview-open-month --run RUN --out PREVIEW/10-judge

RUN is the loop run (the parent of --out). This step reads only step 08's
manifest, RUN/08-verify/verified.json, and the files it lists for the steps it
shows as `reproduced`. When RUN holds no 08-verify/, it judges the population's
committed stand-in run instead (DIR/step10/run, dated in a closed month), and
its detail says the records are that stand-in, not this run's:

  manifest   08's finding passes steps/finding.py's check and names
             verified.json in its proof with the sha256 the file has. The
             as-of instant is 08's finding `finished`.
  window     12 whole closed calendar months before the as-of month, never
             rolling (the pinned pack's window.months). A record is a primary record file (binding.json `records`) that 08 lists
             for a reproduced step of one of the pack's kinds (05 deals, 06
             settlements, 07 asks, 09 disputes) whose step finished in the
             window. Its bytes must still match 08's digest. A file 08 does
             not list, and a record outside the window, is refused, not read,
             and named in detail. A step 08 did not reproduce is outside the
             window, with a not_checked entry.
  pack       deterministic, no model: one claim per term of the step's kind,
             citing every record of the step; the verdict is recomputed from
             the result 08 re-derived (PASS met, FAIL not_met, NOT_CHECKED
             not_evaluable). The served_named_model term reads "provider states" where no record
             carries model_attestation. On live, a 05 whose proof keeps the nodes' own chains is
             decided instead by the pinned pack's own evaluator over them (loop#157). 09's referee Result is cited and
             counted as found, never judged again. The pack is the one versions.lock
             pins (`inference-deals`), fetched by 10-judge.setup.sh; not fetched is NOT_CHECKED.
  seal       a fresh book under the population's judge key: on rehearsal the
             committed TEST key (population/rehearsal/step10/keys); on live the
             lab's own judge key, read from LOOP_JUDGE_KEY (default
             $LAB_DIR/judge/judge.pem, never in this tree), whose public half
             is the committed population/live/step10/keys/judge.pub.pem. It
             signs the book's checkpoints too. Each record is published as a
             capsule whose payload is {step, path, sha256}; `capsulectl book
             result build` seals one Result per step and a roll-up Result
             citing them; `capsulectl book disclose` writes one bundle per
             Result.
  judge      on the bundles alone, offline:
               verify    each bundle is VALID under `capsulectl verify
                         --bundle` (an empty config), and every record in it
                         is under the repository's judge key;
               complete  the finer Results cite every record in the window;
               exact     every record they cite is in the window;
               rollup    the roll-up cites exactly the finer Results, each the
                         root of a VALID bundle.

--preview-open-month (evidence-network/loop#242) judges the open month instead: the calendar month containing 08's
as-of instant, e.g. 2026-10-01 to 2026-11-01, with the same pinned pack and the same judge key. It is a look at records
before their month closes, never a baseline result: the baseline window stays 12 whole closed months. It reads RUN
(--run, which holds 08-verify/, never the stand-in) and writes only --out, which may not lie inside RUN or findings/;
every finding it writes has a detail that starts with finding.PREVIEW, which the ecosystem gate refuses. Its
window.json names the sha256 of the manifest it judged, so step 11 can refuse a preview of another run.

PASS when every check held and every step 08 lists was reproduced; FAIL when a
check did not hold; NOT_CHECKED when the window holds no record, a step is not
reproduced, or the tools or 08's manifest are missing. The design is
steps/10-judge.md. Exit 0 once the finding is written, whatever the result.
"""
